course: dictionary
lesson: 5931
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word martin is a good example. It can be a small bird, a boy's name, or the name of a saint. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: Capital letters give you a clue. A bird's name is written with a small m, as in «house martin». A person's name starts with a capital M, as in «Martin Luther». Ask yourself: is this a thing, a person, or a place? Then check your choice by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: «In 1517 Martin Luther, a German monk, criticised the Church for selling forgiveness.» Here Martin is a person, because a monk can criticise something and a bird cannot. Luther is a surname, so Martin is a first name. Read on and the clues will show you which meaning fits.
fact: A martin is a small bird of the swallow family, such as the house martin.
fact: House martins build mud nests under the roofs of houses and fly south in winter.
fact: Martin is a common boy's first name and also a surname.
fact: Saint Martin of Tours was a soldier who cut his cloak in half to share with a freezing beggar; he is remembered for kindness.
fact: A capital M and the words around it help you tell the bird from the name.
exercise: «In 1517 Martin Luther, a German monk, criticised the Church.» What is Martin here? | *A person's name | A small bird of the swallow family | A church building | A kind of mud nest
exercise: «Martins built a mud nest under the roof and flew south in winter.» What is a martin here? | A saint who shared his cloak | A boy called Martin | A soldier from Tours | *A small bird
exercise: «Martin was shot, and his wound healed.» Is Martin a bird or a name? How do you know? | *A name, because a person can be shot and heal | A saint, because saints always heal | A bird, because it has a capital M | A bird, because birds can be shot and heal
test: «Martin Luther King Jr led the civil rights movement for equality.» What does Martin mean here? | A soldier who cut his cloak | Mud nest | *A person's name | A kind of swallow that flies south
test: «The house martin built its nest under the eaves.» What is the house martin? | A boy's first name | *A small bird | A printing press | A saint of Tours
exam: «Saint Martin of Tours shared his cloak with a freezing beggar.» What does this sentence tell you about Martin? | Martin is a kind of printing press | Martin is a mud nest under a roof | Martin was a bird that kept the beggar warm | *Martin is a name, here for a saint remembered for kindness
